**Factorization-planner library layer: mixed-radix Stockham (radix-4/8 thresholded, conjugate-pair dense primes) + unpadded Rader (65537/1021) + smooth-padded Bluestein (10007→20480, 100003→262144) + across-batch 8-lane execution (≤1K); best wallaby: L=32 0.096 µs B=1 / 0.064 µs B=512 (65537: ~1150 µs B=1), rel L2 ≤ 4.4e-15 on all 26 graded cells (tol 1e-12).**

Notes for the monitor: the Ice Lake reservation was dead all round (job 440299 not running, heartbeat stale), so per instructions I submitted nothing to slurm and replicated tryout.sh's exact build/run/check by hand on wallaby (core-pinned, interleaved A/Bs for all design decisions — wallaby cores vary 2x, so only the same-core A/Bs were trusted). Coverage went from 0 cells to all 52 (`fft1d_supports` now accepts any L≥1); all 26 non-chained cells PASS at ≤4.4e-15 and the chained map gate passes (3.8e-14 vs anchor 2.7e-15). The strategy record in `strategies/d1_planner.md` documents the two failed approaches with killing numbers (flat radix-8 usage, lanes above 1K), the survey techniques adopted, and the next-round list headed by nested Rader for 100003 and four-step at 16384+.
